    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 8,
    "title": "State what happens to a specific object",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk3-ba-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "State what happens to a specific object",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "After 把 + the known object, give the action an informative result or destination. 写清楚 states the result of writing; 写进… states where the information is put. For a transfer, put 给 + recipient after the verb. Place 没有 before 把; completed-event 了 belongs with the predicate, not immediately after 把.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我把时间和地点写清楚。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ bǎ shíjiān hé dìdiǎn xiě qīngchu 。",
                "meaning": "I write the time and place clearly.",
                "audio": "ac89811c73c4e9061487f3571129e7b5effee74616e516f5d5414cf4d0b97100"
              },
              {
                "text": "我把新地点写进一封邮件。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ bǎ xīn dìdiǎn xiě jìn yī fēng yóujiàn 。",
                "meaning": "I put the new location into an email.",
                "audio": "336d716b581ff75a1398b7124accdbb083d3e039fe9d391cfa541379d11693e7"
              },
              {
                "text": "我把书送给他了。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ bǎ shū sòng gěi tā le 。",
                "meaning": "I gave the book to him.",
                "audio": "e22b3b0040bbc4026eb789f498ef4507b2cbeca7c5a7d1f01d433cec340ce887"
              },
              {
                "text": "我没有把书送给他。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ méiyǒu bǎ shū sòng gěi tā 。",
                "meaning": "I did not give the book to him.",
                "audio": "accdea21000bfd83821e4721446aaf6a441a690e8c8da492f6a4081dd59c0a82"
              }
            ]
          },
